Trees:
Properties:

Trees are non linear data structures.It has different kind of nodes which are stored separately(Arrays are linear data structure which store values one after the other)

Trees are also known as hierarchial datastructures: A single node inside a tree can be connected to various other nodes.It is known as hierarchy

Each node inside a  tree has 0 or more than 0 children
The node have only one parent except root(starting point of tree/the most top level of tree)

Nodes cannot have cycles(it means,there will be only parent of each node,not more then 1,if it have more then 1 parent,it will become a cycle which is not possible in tree)

If we have to travel one node to another node,it will have exactly 1 path (see one travel path image)

No 2 parents can have same child (exactly same as each node has only 1 parent)

------------------------------------------------------
Why we need trees when we have arrays and Linked list?
Not every type of data can be stored inside an array or inside linked list.Suppose,we have to store hierarchial data,then trees are the best data structure for that

Examples:
a)File Systems( in our laptops,data is distributed like trees,like we have desktop folder ,inside that we have document & download folder,so file system is best example of trees)

b)Html Dom
c)Databases
d)Hierarchial data
e)Virtual dom in react
